DECISION
AR-H113 is POSITIVE WITH AN UNCONDITIONAL-PANIC FAILURE.

Supported synthetically:

- global emergency broadcast is highly resource expensive;
- unconditional waves also spread emergency state far beyond need;
- provenance identity alone does not constrain wave spread;
- local relevance gating preserves full tested threat protection;
- local gating dramatically reduces response and relay cost;
- false credentialed sources remain tightly localized when relevance is revalidated at each hop;
- extra anticipatory wave depth is not automatically useful.

Not demonstrated:

- learned relevance cues;
- adversarial false local precursor;
- multiple interacting emergency fronts;
- resource-constrained wave competition;
- continuous threat severity;
- real emergency actions.

